## What I Learned Today

Today I learned how the raw UWB CIR measurements are stored inside the dataset and how they must be converted from hexadecimal strings into numerical arrays before they can be processed by a neural network.

I also learned that validating the dataset is an essential step before model training because corrupted CIR measurements can interrupt the preprocessing pipeline and negatively affect the learning process.

---

## Personal Reflection

Before today, I thought preparing the dataset would be a simple loading step.

However, I realized that a considerable amount of work is required before building the AutoEncoder. Even a small number of corrupted CIR samples can stop the preprocessing process if they are not detected properly.

This stage helped me better understand the structure of the experimental dataset used in the paper and increased my confidence in reproducing the remaining parts of the proposed framework.

